Johnny read her scepticism. \'93Believe me when I tell you, detective, I learned something that day. The Elvi may appear as meek bartenders and buffoonish karaoke clowns, but\'97\'94 He went into \'91splainer mode. \'93There\'92s something particular in their warranties, which is: never get an ELVIS angry.\'94  \
\'93Are you telling me, the staff of a nightclub... what are you telling me?\'94\
\'93The PAPER agents didn\'92t stand a chance.\'94  \
\'93What? Come on\'85\'94\
\'93No, hear me out. The Elvi can 
\f2\i fight
\f1\i0 . First, all of them are packing weapons. They surprised the PAPER agents by shooting out all the chandeliers. They threw pool balls, and they attacked with cue sticks and pistol butts. They shot up a bunch of bathrooms and attacked with chunks of broken toilet bowls.\'94\
\'93And now they have tanks.\'94\
Johnny blanched.  \
\'93Any idea where they acquired those?\'94 Hayley pursued.\
\'93Um, none whatsoever.\'94 Johnny swallowed.  \
It would have been easy to pin the tanks on Eloise Shakti, or any of the lesser arms dealers. That Johnny choked revealed much.  \
\'93What happened next?\'94\
\'93Sarah called out to me. She was trying to fight off several of the Elvi. She said something, then they all looked over at Chantara, as if waiting for instructions. He bounced on the balls of his feet, then approached calmly, like he was in charge. I ran to Sarah, to save her, but I was too late. They forced her through an exit, with Chantara following, not a care in the world. He even saluted me as he left. Then I too was captured and forced to the ground. That\'92s the last thing I remember. When I came to, the place was empty, completely abandoned.\'94
